her pietro maximoff  aka quicksilver  for marvel studios this shared custody  agreement meant that they could use  wanda but  couldn't make her a mutant or obviously  the daughter of magneto  thus while wanda still has a twin  brother named pietro maximoff in the mcu  her parents are normal human beings  another part of her origin story that  was altered  the mcu's version of wanda hails from  the european country of sokovia  rather than her original comic book  country of origin transia  though the names of the countries have  changed sokovia bears more than a  passing resemblance to wanda's original  homeland  like transient sokovia is a fictional  eastern european country  rife with political turmoil making it a  subtle nod to wanda maximoff's original  home for comics fans  not all superheroes start out as  superheroes  some start out like tony stark arrogance  people so blinded by their own wealth  that they can't see how their actions  affect others  other superheroes begin their journeys  as outright super villains  like wanda maximoff she and her brother  pietro began their time in the marvel  cinematic universe as  voluntary human guinea pigs for the  terrorist organization known as hydra  these experiments gave them both their  superpowers and  they eventually joined forces with the  diabolical robot ultron  as his super-powered henchmen in their  time working for ultron  wanda and her brother tormented the  avengers and helped lay the groundwork  for the maniacal robot's plan for world  domination while this  is different from the duo's origin story  in the comics  it isn't a complete change wanda also  started out as a villain there as well  there she and pietro as the children of  magneto were  critical figures in the brotherhood of  mutants and frequently fought the x-men  much like their film incarnations though  wanda and pietro didn't stay villainous  for long  how could you how could i what you said  we would destroy the avengers make a  better world  it will be better in both mediums they  eventually turned against their evil  masters  and went on to work for the avengers  just as  comics readers always suspected they  would the  suburban new jersey setting of one  division is a gift that keeps on giving  on the surface it allows the show to pay  homage to classic sitcoms  many of which also take place in the  suburbs it works for the show but  it wasn't just invented for tv this  superhero duo's new jersey roots  actually go all the way back to an  offbeat storyline in the 1985 comic  series the vision and the scarlet witch  in that series the couple moves to the  new jersey suburbs after getting married  to enjoy a life together  unfortunately it isn't that easy the  locals aren't happy with a human android  marriage happening in their community  the source of conflict in the vision in  scarlet witch is  more mundane than the supernatural  goings-on that fuel the plot of one  division  but putting the pair in west view adds a  connective tissue to wanda and vision's  prior comic book series  as well as 2016's vision series which  saw the character of vision once again  retreating to the suburbs with the new  synthezoid family  in the mcu hawkeye and wanda maximoff  have developed a close bond  since meeting an avengers age of ultron  their first big meeting didn't seem to  signal that dynamic though as it  entailed wanda still working as a minion  of ultron  trying to sneak up on hawkeye only for  the archer to plug an electric  arrow onto her forehead however the two  superheroes grew closer once wanda  defected to the avengers  this was solidified by the climax of age  of ultron  which saw hawkeye giving wanda a big  speech about what it means to be an  avenger  okay look the city is flying we're  fighting an army of robots  and i have a bow and arrow none of this  makes sense  his rapport with wanda took on a  paternal sense of protection after her  brother pietro sacrificed himself to  save hawkeye  just like that she had lost the only  family she had left in the world  so hawkeye stepped in to help her feel  like she still had somewhere she  belonged  the pair has also had a close bond in  the comics though  it's been more complicated there instead  of having paternal feelings for wanda in  the comics  hawkeye sees her more as a romantic  interest  at least until vision shows up in her  life while their relationship has been  altered for the movies  hawkeye and wanda's closeness in the mcu  echoes the comics that came before it  though one division marks the first time  wanda maximoff has used her superpowers  to create a persistent alternate reality  in the marvel cinematic universe it's  something she's accomplished in the  comics before  more than once her abilities in this  department were most famously the crux  of the comic book story line house event  which was penned by brian michael bendis  in 2005.  here wanda much like in one division is  in a period of deep emotional distress  though in house of m her grief is the  result of losing her children  not losing vision to cope with her  crushing  sadness wanda decides to escape by  creating her own  alternate reality this decision doesn't  just impact wanda though  it sends the entire marvel universe into  chaos creating a world  run by mutants under the cold rule of  the family of magneto  when the rest of the heroes in the  marvel universe wake up to what's going  on  they're forced to come together to stop  wanda at any cost and set the world  right again looking at house of m's  broad strokes it's clear  wand division takes cues from this  comic's event including the emphasis on  wanda navigating very  real emotional problems through her  superpowers  there are clear and major differences  between the comics and the show but the  similarities between the two  are impossible to miss check out one of  our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

